# Corrects the eggcorn `past of least resistance` -> `path of least resistance`.
expr main <(past of least resistance), past>

let message "The idiom is `path of least resistance`."
let description "Corrects the eggcorn `past of least resistance` to `path of least resistance`."
let kind "Grammar"
let becomes "path"
let strategy "MatchCase"

# True positives

test "It shifts the past of least resistance toward data attacks." "It shifts the path of least resistance toward data attacks."
test "Attackers follow the past of least resistance." "Attackers follow the path of least resistance."
test "Water takes the past of least resistance." "Water takes the path of least resistance."
test "The past of least resistance is chosen." "The path of least resistance is chosen."
test "They chose the past of least resistance." "They chose the path of least resistance."
test "Past of least resistance wins." "Path of least resistance wins."
test "Electricity follows the past of least resistance." "Electricity follows the path of least resistance."
test "Consider the past of least resistance here." "Consider the path of least resistance here."
test "Seeking the past of least resistance." "Seeking the path of least resistance."
test "It was a past of least resistance approach." "It was a path of least resistance approach."

# False positives / true negatives

allows "They took the path of least resistance."
allows "In the past, resistance was futile."
allows "The line of least resistance is different."
allows "His past of failures haunted him."
allows "The past of the company is murky."
